==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
I.M. Phace on his own is not a problem, but things get messy once Gory Darks get in the way. Midrange Gory Dark counters such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] are less effective in this stage, for they tend to walk into I.M. Phace's attacks and get picked off. This problem can be circumvented by allowing the Gory Darks to push your frontline out of I.M. Phace's range. From there, any of your attackers should be capable of dealing with the Gory Darks. An alternative strategy is to destroy the base before I.M. Phace spawns. As long as you can deal with the Gory Darks, just spam fast cats to break the base first.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Ring Girl Cat is an effective enough unit to deal with the Doge Darks and works well for the Dark Otters. Use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] to deliver chip damage to I.M. Phace, in addition to [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] such as [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]] to deal with the Scissoroos.

==='''Chapter 3 '''===
This stage is relatively straightforward. It is best to bring 3-4 meatshields, as the Scissoroos and Shadow Boxer Ks would otherwise cripple your defenses. Ring Girl Cat is great at killing the Dark enemies, however her attacks may get interrupted if enemies are pushing too quickly. Bring units that outrange I.M. Phace, such as Dragon Cat and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]]. Anti-Alien crowd-controllers like Castaway Cat are worth bringing to keep the Scissoroos in check. If you own her, [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] is an excellent counter to this stage, as she can juggle the main threats while comfortably outranging I.M. Phace.

